    "meaning_en": "use several adjectives together",
    "example": "It's a small, cheap, old car."
   }
  ],
  "grammar": [
   {
    "title": "It's + adjective / It's a + adjective + noun",
    "explanation_ar": "الصفة في الإنجليزية تأتي بعد be (It's big) أو قبل الاسم (a big TV)، وليس بعد الاسم كما في العربية. الصفة لا تتغير مع الجمع: big TVs.",
    "explanation_en": "Adjectives go after \"be\" (It's big) or before the noun (a big TV). They never take -s.",
    "examples": [
     "It's big.",
     "It's a big TV.",
     "They're cheap bags."
    ]
   },
   {
    "title": "Opposite adjectives",
    "explanation_ar": "تعلّم الصفات في أزواج متضادة لتتذكرها بسهولة: big/small، new/old، expensive/cheap، heavy/light.",
    "explanation_en": "Learn adjectives in pairs of opposites.",
    "examples": [
     "big ≠ small",
     "new ≠ old",
     "expensive ≠ cheap",
     "heavy ≠ light"
    ]
   },
   {
    "title": "a / an with adjectives",
    "explanation_ar": "نختار a أو an حسب أول صوت في الكلمة التي بعدها مباشرة: a TV لكن an expensive TV، و an old bag.",
    "explanation_en": "Choose \"a\" or \"an\" by the first sound of the next word: an expensive TV, an old bag.",
    "examples": [
     "It's a new phone.",
     "It's an old phone.",
     "It's an expensive watch."
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
